1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,975
NBA All-Star Weekend Debuts Team World vs. Team USA Format.

2
00:00:04,925 --> 00:00:19,225
The NBA unveiled a groundbreaking Team World versus Team United States format at the 2026 All-Star Weekend in Los Angeles, replacing the traditional East versus West and captains-draft models that had defined the event for decades.

3
00:00:19,225 --> 00:00:29,350
The change reflected the league's increasingly global roster, which now features a record 135 international players from 41 countries and territories.

4
00:00:29,350 --> 00:00:39,662
Team World, led by MVP candidate Shai Gilgeous-Alexander and Luka Doncic, pushed Team USA to the limit in a high-scoring contest at Crypto.com Arena.

5
00:00:39,662 --> 00:00:50,225
The new format energized fans and players alike, with national pride and international bragging rights adding competitive edge to an event critics had labeled as lacking defense.

6
00:00:50,225 --> 00:00:58,687
The weekend also featured the Rising Stars Challenge, Three-Point Contest, and Slam Dunk Contest, all of which drew strong ratings.

7
00:00:58,687 --> 00:01:07,600
Notably, LeBron James was not voted an All-Star starter for the first time in two decades, a symbolic passing of the torch to a new generation.

8
00:01:07,600 --> 00:01:13,275
Commissioner Adam Silver hailed the weekend as "a celebration of basketball's global reach.

